  [1mDesign[0m

  [1mStack[0m

  Vanilla JS ES modules, no framework, no build step, [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m for persistence. A prototype's job is to be readable
  and changeable; a bundler and a framework would be more infrastructure than feature here. All logic lives in plain
  modules importable by a test runner directly.

  [1mData model[0m

  [36musers[39m:  [{ id, name, color }]                        [32m// 3-4, seeded[39m
  [36mtasks[39m:  [{ id, title, status, assigneeId, dueDate, [36mwatcherIds[39m: [] }]
  [36mevents[39m: [{ id, taskId, type, actorId, [34mfrom[39m, to, at }] [32m// append-only[39m
  [36mread[39m:   { [userId]: [34mSet[39m<eventId> }
  [36msession[39m:{ currentUserId, simulatorOn }

  [38;5;153mstatus[39m is [38;5;153mtodo | in-progress | done[39m; [38;5;153mtype[39m is [38;5;153mstatus | assignee | dueDate[39m.

  [1mModules[0m

